---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="description" content="Build and compare definitions of New Hampshire education aid per student across district schools, charter schools, EFAs, and SWEPT from FY2016 through FY2027.">
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/NH%20DB%20Logo.svg">
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/NH%20DB%20Logo.svg">
    <title>Explore New Hampshire Education Aid Per Student</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <TopNav />
<main>
<header class="education-report-hero" id="top">
<div class="shell hero-grid">
<div>
<p class="eyebrow">New Hampshire education funding</p>
<h1>Explore New Hampshire education aid.</h1>
<p class="dek">Choose the aid and students to count. The tool applies the same choices from FY2016 through FY2027 and marks missing data.</p>
<nav class="jump-links" aria-label="Jump to report section">
<a href="#explorer">Build a calculation</a>
<a href="#glossary">Funding dictionary</a>
<a href="#programs">Program totals</a>
<a href="#sources">Sources &amp; downloads</a>
<a href="#community-updates">Community updates</a>
</nav>
</div>
<aside class="hero-verdict" aria-label="How to use this page">
<span class="verdict-label">Use the tool in three steps</span>
<ol>
  <li>Choose the aid.</li>
  <li>Choose the students.</li>
  <li>Compare years.</li>
</ol>
<span>The page starts with all actual programs, excluding SWEPT, in the latest complete year.</span>
</aside>
</div>
</header>

<section class="explorer-band" id="explorer" aria-labelledby="explorer-heading" data-funding-explorer>
  <div class="shell section">
    <div class="section-heading light-heading explorer-heading">
      <p class="section-number">01</p>
      <div>
        <h2 id="explorer-heading">Choose what counts</h2>
        <p>Select one district measure, add other programs, and see the total and per-student amount.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="preset-row" aria-label="Calculation presets">
      <span>Start with a definition:</span>
      <button type="button" data-preset="all-programs" aria-pressed="true">All programs · no SWEPT</button>
      <button type="button" data-preset="district-only" aria-pressed="false">District grant</button>
      <button type="button" data-preset="with-swept" aria-pressed="false">District grant + SWEPT</button>
      <button type="button" data-preset="calculated-cost" aria-pressed="false">Formula cost</button>
    </div>

    <div class="explorer-layout">
      <form class="explorer-controls" data-controls>
        <fieldset>
          <legend><span>1</span> Choose one district measure</legend>
          <label class="choice-row">
            <input type="radio" name="district-measure" value="districtGrant" checked>
            <span><strong>District grant paid</strong><small>Actual grant, excluding SWEPT</small></span>
          </label>
          <label class="choice-row nested-choice" data-district-addons-row>
            <input type="checkbox" data-district-addons checked>
            <span><strong>Differential aid + extraordinary-needs + hold-harmless grants</strong><small>Turn off to use base adequacy aid</small></span>
          </label>
          <label class="choice-row">
            <input type="radio" name="district-measure" value="calculatedCost">
            <span><strong>Formula cost</strong><small>Base adequacy plus differential aid</small></span>
          </label>
          <label class="choice-row">
            <input type="radio" name="district-measure" value="none">
            <span><strong>No district aid</strong><small>Show charter or EFA programs alone</small></span>
          </label>
        </fieldset>

        <fieldset>
          <legend><span>2</span> Other funding to include</legend>
          <label class="choice-row">
            <input type="checkbox" data-funding="swept">
            <span><strong>SWEPT</strong><small>Locally collected and retained property-tax revenue</small></span>
          </label>
          <label class="choice-row">
            <input type="checkbox" data-funding="charterDirect" checked>
            <span><strong>Charter direct aid</strong><small>State payment sent directly to charter schools</small></span>
          </label>
          <label class="choice-row">
            <input type="checkbox" data-funding="charterSped" checked>
            <span><strong>Charter special-education aid</strong><small>Charter-related cost paid to responsible districts</small></span>
          </label>
          <label class="choice-row">
            <input type="checkbox" data-funding="efaPayments" checked>
            <span><strong>EFA scheduled payments</strong><small>Education Freedom Account payments; program began in FY2022</small></span>
          </label>
        </fieldset>

        <fieldset>
          <legend><span>3</span> Students in the denominator</legend>
          <label class="auto-match">
            <input type="checkbox" data-auto-match checked>
            <span><strong>Match students to selected programs</strong><small>Recommended for a meaningful per-student result</small></span>
          </label>
          <div class="student-choices">
            <label><input type="checkbox" data-student="districtAdm" checked> District ADM</label>
            <label><input type="checkbox" data-student="charterAdm" checked> Charter ADM</label>
            <label><input type="checkbox" data-student="efaMembership" checked> EFA membership</label>
          </div>
          <p class="manual-note" data-manual-note>Turn off matching to choose the student population manually.</p>
        </fieldset>
      </form>

      <div class="explorer-output">
        <div class="formula-card">
          <div>
            <span>How this calculation works</span>
            <a href="#glossary">Definitions ↓</a>
          </div>
          <p data-formula>—</p>
        </div>

        <figure class="trend-card spend-chart-card">
          <figcaption>
            <div>
              <span>Selected programs, every year</span>
              <strong>Total spending by program</strong>
            </div>
            <small>Each bar stacks the selected programs. Incomplete years are marked instead of treating missing data as zero.</small>
          </figcaption>
          <div class="chart-legend" data-spend-legend aria-label="Selected funding programs"></div>
          <svg data-spend-chart viewBox="0 0 760 286" role="img" aria-labelledby="spend-title spend-description">
            <title id="spend-title">Total selected education spending by program and fiscal year</title>
            <desc id="spend-description">A stacked bar chart that updates when funding selections change.</desc>
          </svg>
        </figure>

        <figure class="trend-card">
          <figcaption>
            <div>
              <span>Same definition, every year</span>
              <strong>Per-student trend</strong>
            </div>
            <small>Hover or focus a point to see the year and aid per student. Gaps mean data is unavailable.</small>
          </figcaption>
          <svg data-trend-chart viewBox="0 0 760 270" role="img" aria-labelledby="trend-title trend-description">
            <title id="trend-title">Education aid per selected student by fiscal year</title>
            <desc id="trend-description">A line chart that updates when funding and student selections change.</desc>
          </svg>
        </figure>

        <details class="trend-table-details" open>
          <summary>See the calculation for every year</summary>
          <div class="table-wrap">
            <table class="explorer-table">
              <thead><tr><th>Year</th><th class="numeric">Selected funding</th><th class="numeric">Selected students</th><th class="numeric">Per student</th><th>Coverage</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody data-trend-table></tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="shell section glossary-section" id="glossary" aria-labelledby="glossary-heading">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="section-number">02</p>
    <div>
      <h2 id="glossary-heading">Funding terms</h2>
      <p>These terms describe different formulas, payments, taxes, programs, and student counts.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="glossary-grid">
    <article id="glossary-base-adequacy">
      <span>Formula building block</span>
      <h3>Base adequacy</h3>
      <p>The starting amount for each district student in the adequacy formula. It is only one part of the formula cost.</p>
    </article>
    <article id="glossary-differential-aid">
      <span>Student-need additions</span>
      <h3>Differential aid</h3>
      <p>Added formula amounts for student needs, including income eligibility, special education, and English-learner status. They are included in formula cost and in the district-grant add-on toggle.</p>
    </article>
    <article id="glossary-calculated-cost">
      <span>District formula</span>
      <h3>Formula cost</h3>
      <p>Base adequacy plus differential aid. It is a formula result, not the amount paid to districts.</p>
    </article>
    <article id="glossary-district-grant">
      <span>District payment</span>
      <h3>District grant paid</h3>
      <p>The actual district grant after local calculations and adjustments. In this tool it excludes SWEPT.</p>
    </article>
    <article id="glossary-swept">
      <span>Property tax</span>
      <h3>SWEPT</h3>
      <p>The Statewide Education Property Tax is collected and kept locally. Some totals include it and others do not.</p>
    </article>
    <article id="glossary-charter">
      <span>Program</span>
      <h3>Charter-school aid</h3>
      <p>Direct aid goes to charter schools. Charter special-education aid goes to responsible public districts. The tool lists each once.</p>
    </article>
    <article id="glossary-efa">
      <span>Program</span>
      <h3>Education Freedom Accounts</h3>
      <p>State-funded accounts for eligible education expenses outside a traditional district-school placement. Data begins in FY2022.</p>
    </article>
    <article id="glossary-students">
      <span>Denominator</span>
      <h3>ADM and payment membership</h3>
      <p>District and charter files use average daily membership (ADM). EFA files use payment membership. Match the student count to the selected aid.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
  <aside class="definition-caution">
    <strong>How the district-grant toggle works.</strong>
    <p>Checked uses the final district grant paid. Unchecked uses base adequacy aid. Formula cost remains a separate measure and already includes differential aid.</p>
  </aside>
</section>
<section class="programs-band" id="programs" aria-labelledby="programs-heading">
<div class="shell section">
<div class="section-heading">
<p class="section-number">03</p>
<div>
<h2 id="programs-heading">Where the money and students went</h2>
<p>Statewide totals include district schools, charter schools, and EFAs.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="impact-grid">
<article>
<span>FY2016–FY2025</span>
<strong>$75.0m</strong>
<p>Growth in charter-related and EFA costs—36.6% of the total non-SWEPT increase.</p>
</article>
<article>
<span>FY2023–FY2025</span>
<strong>−$7.5m</strong>
<p>Change in the main district grant while charter and EFA costs rose by $31.9 million.</p>
</article>
<article>
<span>FY2025</span>
<strong>$98.3m</strong>
<p>Combined charter-related and EFA costs—12.3% of total non-SWEPT aid.</p>
</article>
<article>
<span>FY2025–FY2026</span>
<strong>+84.8%</strong>
<p>EFA membership growth; scheduled payments rose from $30.1 million to $51.6 million.</p>
</article>
</div>
